But Jesus didn't answer even a word, not to a single accusation. And the governor remained very much astonished.
It was the custom of the governor on Easter to release a certain number of prisoners. The people had influence in deciding who should be released.
At that moment they had a well-known prisoner called Barabbas.
When the crowd was gathered, Pilate addressed them, saying, "Whom do you want me to release for you: Barabbas, or Jesus who is called Christ?"
Pilate knew that the leaders were jealous. He knew that this was the reason they had handed Jesus over to him.
